.TH RUSTFETCH 1 "2026-11-15" "rustfetch 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustfetch \- lightweight system information tool for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustfetch
.RI [ COMMAND ] " " [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustfetch
displays essential system information in a terminal with a distro-aware ASCII logo.
It reads information from local Linux interfaces and environment variables.
It does not use network access, telemetry, or background services.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR (default) ", " info
Show full system information.
.TP
.B cpu
Show CPU model.
.TP
.B gpu
Show GPU information.
.TP
.B memory
Show memory usage.
.TP
.B disk
Show root filesystem disk usage.
.TP
.B os
Show operating system name.
.TP
.B uptime
Show uptime.
.TP
.B logo
Show only the detected distro logo.
.TP
.BI "logo " name
Show full system information with a specific logo.
.TP
.B "logo list"
List all available logo names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-distro " " \fINAME\fR
Use a specific distro logo for full info output.
.TP
.B \-\-config
Show configuration path.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output full info as JSON (valid with full info output).
.TP
.B \-\-logo
Alias for
.B logo
command.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json ,
the following fields are emitted: \fBos\fR, \fBdistro_id\fR, \fBkernel\fR, \fBhostname\fR, \fBusername\fR, \fBuptime\fR, \fBshell\fR, \fBde\fR, \fBwm\fR, \fBterminal\fR, \fBcpu\fR, \fBgpu\fR, \fBmemory\fR, \fBdisk\fR, \fBarchitecture\fR.
The \fBgpu\fR field may be \fBnull\fR when unavailable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command or option.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rustfetch/config.toml
Configuration path reported by \fB--config\fR when \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR is set.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustfetch/config.toml
Fallback configuration path reported by \fB--config\fR.
.PP
The current version reports the configuration path but does not require or parse a configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B rustfetch
Show full system information.
.TP
.B rustfetch --distro nixos
Show full system information with the NixOS logo.
.TP
.B rustfetch cpu
Show CPU model.
.TP
.B rustfetch --json
Show full system information as JSON.
.SH NOTES
GPU detection is best-effort and may fall back to vendor/device identifiers.
Disk usage is reported for the root filesystem.
Desktop environment, window manager/session, terminal, and shell values depend on the runtime environment.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project repository: https://github.com/q7xk/rustfetch
.SH AUTHORS
Rustfetch contributors.
